WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.566 line:-3
Now I need to adjust the textile heel strap

2
00:00:02.766 --> 00:00:06.200 line:-3
so that the size fits me. For example,

3
00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:09.966 line:-3
I set my Combo Ski between size S and M.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.566 line:-3
So I loosen the plastic buckle,

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.133 line:-3
and adjust the strap to fit comfortably.

6
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.366 line:-3
I do the same on the other Combo Ski.

7
00:00:29.566 --> 00:00:31.933 line:-3
Now I put the Combo Ski on my right foot,

8
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.933 line:-3
The R mark is

9
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.566 line:-3
on the upper Velcro strap.

10
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.700 line:-3
I tighten the straps firmly,

11
00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:50.566 line:-3
using the buckle.

12
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.200 line:-3
The front strap over the toes,

13
00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:00.133 line:-3
then the upper Velcro strap.

14
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:09.333 line:-3
I do the same on the left foot.

15
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.183 line:-3
While standing, I tighten the straps,

16
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:14.500 line:-3
so that Combo Ski feels like
a solid part of the boot.

17
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:20.800 line:-3
I check the heel strap
used to adjust the size.

18
00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.166 line:-3
The upper strap

19
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:24.500 line:-3
can sit either on the boot,

20
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.966 line:-3
or directly on the leg. Both are correct.
